From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 06:09:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11014/11171] Record the pattern: the live eval keeps not
 recording what consumers need

Three instances in three days -- trajectory_supervisor, generator_channels, and
now induction_attempts -- each discovered the same way, by a consumer running,
failing, and only then revealing the field was never emitted. The first two are
fixed; the third is deliberately left, because adding it as a third one-off is
the fourth instance waiting to happen.

The shape does not vary. The runtime object has the data, exactly one consumer
reads it, that consumer is frozen or shadow-mode or otherwise unusable, and the
live path records nothing. Nobody learns this until something downstream comes
back empty. arc_scored_path_lever_harness.py, frozen on a retired model pin, was
the sole reader for both of the first two.

Prose will not hold this. The mechanical form is a join with no model in it: for
each field a consumer reads from a run artifact, assert that some artifact in
results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs/ actually contains it. It fails the day a
consumer is written against a field nobody emits, which is when fixing it is
free, rather than months later at the cost of seven GPU-hours.

The generalisable half is the sentence worth keeping: a diagnostic with exactly
one reader is one frozen harness away from being unrecorded, and that state is
invisible until it costs something.

Also closes a standing caveat. The conductor re-exec'd onto 1be84f6514e7, which
matches disk and HEAD, so REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-3 and -4 are live rather than
merely committed, and every earlier report saying "live at the next iteration
boundary" can now be read as live.

Written because the pattern had been stated in a commit message and then walked
past, which is the failure mode the never-forget rule exists to catch.

